      "body": "## Motivation\n\nPEFT adapters saved with `use_rslora=True` store that flag in `adapter_config.json` and scale updates by `lora_alpha / sqrt(r)`. SGLang's `LoRAAdapter` always used `lora_alpha / r`, so rsLoRA adapters load silently but apply updates that are `sqrt(r)` times too weak (e.g. 8× at `r=64`).\n\nFixes #40835\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Read `use_rslora` from the PEFT adapter config (default `False`).\n- Compute scaling as `alpha / sqrt(r)` when rsLoRA is enabled, matching PEFT/vLLM.\n- Add a CPU unit test covering standard LoRA, rsLoRA, and the default-off path.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\n```bash\nPYTHONPATH=python python3 -m pytest test/registered/unit/lora/test_rslora_scaling.py -v\n```\n\n3 passed locally (CPU).\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format code & doc strings\n- [x] Add tests\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #35815742140](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35815742140)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #35815741655](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35815741655)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #35815741811](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35815741811)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
